2026-06-11 16:53:33,703 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent received: The AI assistance solution must provide intelligent support to hospital staff in their daily activities, facilitating access to information, improving the quality of written outputs, and reducing processing and documentation times. What AI components and innovation strategies can we propose to meet these requirements, and how will we ensure that our solution is explainable, transparent, and aligned with regulatory guidelines on AI in healthcare?
2026-06-11 16:54:31,147 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-06-11 16:54:31,148 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent answered: To provide intelligent support to hospital staff, we at Faber IA can propose an AI assistance solution that leverages our Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) capabilities. This approach allows us to generate answers grounded in the organisation's own validated documents, such as protocols, internal procedures, and applicable regulation. Our RAG capabilities include hybrid retrieval, re-ranking, query reformulation, multi-document synthesis, structured extraction, and template-guided drafting.

To facilitate access to information, improve written outputs, and reduce processing times, we can implement our AI components in the following ways: 

Firstly, our solution can assist with drafting clinical and administrative content, such as discharge summaries and medical reports, by providing template-guided drafting capabilities. This will help improve the quality of written outputs.

Secondly, to facilitate access to information and reduce processing times, we can implement a retrieval system that allows staff to quickly retrieve relevant information from internal procedures, care protocols, and applicable regulations. Our hybrid retrieval approach combines lexical and semantic search methods to ensure accurate results.

Thirdly, our solution can support medical coding (PMSI/ICD-10) for activity reporting (T2A), which will help reduce documentation times and improve the accuracy of medical records.

To ensure explainability, transparency, and alignment with regulatory guidelines on AI in healthcare, we will implement several measures:

1. **Source citations**: Our solution will provide source citations for all generated content, allowing staff to verify the information and understand the context.
2. **Retrieved passages**: We will display retrieved passages used to generate answers, providing transparency into the decision-making process.
3. **Retrieval trace**: A retrieval trace will be available, showing how the AI system arrived at a particular answer or suggestion.
4. **Every interaction logged**: All interactions with the AI system will be logged for posterior audit, ensuring accountability and compliance with regulatory requirements.

Our approach is aligned with the Haute Autorité de Santé (HAS) guidance on the use of AI in healthcare, which emphasizes the importance of transparency, explainability, and human oversight. By providing a non-decisional support tool that assists hospital staff in their daily activities, we can help improve the quality and safety of care while ensuring compliance with regulatory guidelines.

In terms of innovation strategies, our iterative approach to developing the AI solution will involve close collaboration with hospital staff and experts to ensure that the solution meets their needs and is integrated into existing workflows. This will include corpus selection and curation, retrieval tuning, prompt and template design, and evaluation loops to measure the effectiveness of the solution.

By leveraging our RAG capabilities, providing explainable and transparent AI components, and aligning with regulatory guidelines on AI in healthcare, we can propose a comprehensive AI assistance solution that supports hospital staff in their daily activities while ensuring compliance with relevant regulations.
