2. **Retrieved passages**: We will display retrieved passages used to generate answers, providing transparency into the decision-making process.
3. **Retrieval trace**: A retrieval trace will be available, showing how the AI system arrived at a particular answer or suggestion.
4. **Every interaction logged**: All interactions with the AI system will be logged for posterior audit, ensuring accountability and compliance with regulatory requirements.

Our approach is aligned with the Haute Autorité de Santé (HAS) guidance on the use of AI in healthcare, which emphasizes the importance of transparency, explainability, and human oversight. By providing a non-decisional support tool that assists hospital staff in their daily activities, we can help improve the quality and safety of care while ensuring compliance with regulatory guidelines.

In terms of innovation strategies, our iterative approach to developing the AI solution will involve close collaboration with hospital staff and experts to ensure that the solution meets their needs and is integrated into existing workflows. This will include corpus selection and curation, retrieval tuning, prompt and template design, and evaluation loops to measure the effectiveness of the solution.

By leveraging our RAG capabilities, providing explainable and transparent AI components, and aligning with regulatory guidelines on AI in healthcare, we can propose a comprehensive AI assistance solution that supports hospital staff in their daily activities while ensuring compliance with relevant regulations.
